{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And one who strikes.</b> Because he mentioned \"one who strikes a man and he dies\" (Exodus [21:12]), it was necessary to explain that there is a striking without the death of the one struck, such as striking one's father, and there is one who serves on behalf of another, and on account of the honor of the fathers it was necessary to say: even if he does not strike them but only curses them, he is put to death."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:36:53.022671748Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}